IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Management University Act 2000 (Singapore) -- what the company may award (s 3), the Minister's policy directions
-- (s 3B), who appoints and removes trustees (s 4), what needs the Minister's prior written consent and what happens without it
-- (s 5), how public money may be spent (s 6), access to records and the information offence (s 7), student bodies (s 8), and
-- constituent documents inconsistent with the Act (s 9).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SMUA2000.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the only amendment annotated
-- in the body is [40/2018] (s 5(2)). SSO marked the retrieval "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". Section numbers follow the
-- body; the arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is one line out of step with its headings.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0212 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is short (ss 1-9) and is encoded nearly whole, read from the side of a person who meets it: a
-- buyer or counterparty of the company, anyone asked for records, a student society, a graduand.
-- Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 2 beyond its definitions, s 3A (the accountability and quality-assurance frameworks and
-- external review panels -- duties owed to the Minister with no consequence stated), s 6(1) (the Minister's duty to pay what
-- Parliament provides), s 7(3) (the published summary of financial statements, whose form and frequency the Minister sets), and
-- the content of any Gazette exemption order under s 8(2).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Management University Act 2000`

§§ `3 -- what the university company may confer`

-- s 3: "The function of the university company is to pursue, within the limits of the financial resources available to it, the
-- objects provided by its constituent documents and, in particular, to confer and award degrees, diplomas and certificates,
-- including honorary degrees and other distinctions."
-- The rule below says only whether s 3 NAMES the award. Anything else depends on the constituent documents, which were not
-- deposited; FALSE means "not named in s 3", not "forbidden".
DECLARE Award IS ONE OF
    `a degree`
    `a diploma`
    `a certificate`
    `an honorary degree`
    `another distinction`
    `a licence to practise a profession`

GIVEN `the award` IS AN Award
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 names the award` IF
    CONSIDER `the award`
    WHEN `a licence to practise a profession` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3B -- the Minister's policy directions`

-- s 3B(1): "The Minister may, in consultation with the university company, establish any policies on higher education in
-- Singapore that the Minister thinks fit and may direct the university company to implement those policies."
-- (2): "The university company must comply with any direction given by the Minister under subsection (1)."
-- Reading the consultation as a condition of a valid direction is an INFERENCE from "in consultation with"; the Act states no
-- consequence of a failure to consult.
GIVEN `the Minister established the policy` IS A BOOLEAN, `the company was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister directed implementation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company must implement the policy` IF
    `the Minister established the policy` AND `the company was consulted` AND `the Minister directed implementation`

§§ `4, 5 -- trustees and what needs the Minister's prior written consent`

-- s 4(1): "The Board consists of such number of trustees as the Minister may appoint." (2): "The Minister may, at any time, remove
-- or replace any trustee, or appoint new or additional trustees to the Board."
-- s 5(1): "The prior written consent of the Minister is required for -- (a) the admission of any person as a member of the
-- university company and the removal of any such member; (b) the disposal of the whole or substantially the whole of the
-- university company's undertaking or property; (c) the voluntary winding up of the university company; (d) the addition,
-- deletion or alteration of any provision of the constituent documents ...; and (e) the removal of any trustee from the Board."
-- (2): these apply "in addition to" the Companies Act 1967 and the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 [40/2018].
-- (3): "Any act done or agreement made in contravention of subsection (1) has no effect and is unenforceable at law."
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the company or its members`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor may appoint a trustee` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `the Minister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(2) lets the Minister remove a trustee "at any time". s 5(1)(e) requires the Minister's consent for "the removal of any
-- trustee"; the encoding reads (e) as aimed at a removal by the company or its members (an INFERENCE -- the Minister needs no
-- consent from himself or herself), so such a removal needs the Minister's prior written consent.
GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `has the Minister's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor may remove a trustee` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `the Minister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `has the Minister's prior written consent`

DECLARE CompanyAct IS ONE OF
    `admitting a member of the company`
    `removing a member of the company`
    `selling substantially the whole undertaking`
    `selling one building`
    `voluntarily winding up the company`
    `amending the articles of association`
    `removing a trustee`
    `conferring an honorary degree`
    `entering an ordinary supply contract`

GIVEN `the company act` IS A CompanyAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's prior written consent is required` IF
    CONSIDER `the company act`
    WHEN `selling one building` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `conferring an honorary degree` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `entering an ordinary supply contract` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- "Prior" and "written" are both conditions. The Act says nothing of ratification after the event; this encoding reads s 5(3) as
-- leaving a later consent without effect on an act already done (an INFERENCE from "prior").
GIVEN `the company act` IS A CompanyAct, `consent was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent came before the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act has no effect and is unenforceable` IF
    `the Minister's prior written consent is required` `the company act`
    AND NOT (`consent was in writing` AND `consent came before the act`)

§§ `6 -- money from Parliament`

-- s 6(1): the Minister "must pay to the university company such moneys as Parliament may provide from time to time". (2): "All
-- moneys paid to the university company under subsection (1) may only be applied or expended by the university company for such
-- objects provided by its constituent documents as the Minister may allow."
-- Money from other sources (fees, gifts) is outside s 6(2); the encoding returns TRUE for it, which is a statement about s 6 only.
GIVEN `paid under s 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `an object in the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister allows the object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 permits the spending` IF
    IF `paid under s 6(1)` THEN `an object in the constituent documents` AND `the Minister allows the object` ELSE TRUE

§§ `7 -- access to records and the information offence`

-- s 7(1): the Minister or an authorised person "is entitled, at all reasonable times, to full and free access to all accounting
-- and other records relating, directly or indirectly, to the financial transactions of the university company."
GIVEN `the record relates to the company's financial transactions` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister is entitled to access the record` IF
    `the record relates to the company's financial transactions` AND `at a reasonable time`

-- s 7(2): the Minister or an authorised person "may require ANY person to provide him or her with any information in that
-- person's possession, or to which that person has access", considered necessary for ascertaining (a) whether s 6 moneys were
-- properly applied and (b) "any other matters". The power reaches beyond the company: a supplier, a contractor or a student
-- with the information is "any person".
-- (4): "Any person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with any requirement ... under subsection (2), or who otherwise
-- hinders, obstructs or delays the Minister or an authorised person ... shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000." No imprisonment is provided.
-- Read literally, "without reasonable excuse" governs the failure to comply; the hindering limb follows "or who otherwise" and
-- carries no excuse of its own. That is this encoding's reading, not a decided point.
GIVEN `failed to comply with a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `hindered, obstructed or delayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 7(4) offence is committed` IF
        (`failed to comply with a requirement` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `hindered, obstructed or delayed`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 7(4)` MEANS 1000

GIVEN `the fine imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine is within s 7(4)` IF
    `the fine imposed` >= 0 AND `the fine imposed` <= `the maximum fine under s 7(4)`

§§ `8 -- student bodies`

-- s 8(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act have effect in relation to any
-- student body constituted pursuant to the provisions of the constituent documents of the university company."
-- (2): the Minister charged with the responsibility for societies "may, by order in the Gazette, exempt any student body
-- mentioned in subsection (1) from all or any of the provisions of the Societies Act 1966 subject to any conditions".
-- The rule returns whether s 8(1) applies the Societies Act at all; a partial exemption leaves it applying. A student club NOT
-- constituted under the constituent documents is outside s 8 (the general law of societies is not encoded here).
GIVEN `constituted under the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `wholly exempted by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8 applies the Societies Act to the student body` IF
    `constituted under the constituent documents` AND (NOT `wholly exempted by Gazette order`)

§§ `9 -- the Act prevails over the constituent documents`

-- s 9(1): "Any provision of the constituent documents, or any regulation of the university company made under any provision of
-- the constituent documents, that is inconsistent with any provision of this Act is, to the extent of the inconsistency, void."
-- (2): "Nothing in this Act is to be construed as excusing or exempting the university company from complying with any written
-- law that, apart from this Act, would apply to the university company."
GIVEN `a provision of the constituent documents or a regulation under them` IS A BOOLEAN, `inconsistent with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is void to the extent of the inconsistency` IF
    `a provision of the constituent documents or a regulation under them` AND `inconsistent with this Act`

GIVEN `the other written law would apply apart from this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company must still comply with the other written law` IF
    `the other written law would apply apart from this Act`
